IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sssa-nouns`
IMPORT `sssa-seat`

-- Worked cases for sssa-seat.l4: at least one case per question, with the facts a
-- real person in the seat would state.  Every expected value is written from the
-- text of the Act, beside the case, before the run.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are
-- answers the Act gives; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer on these facts".
-- Numbers standing for amounts that the regulations would prescribe, and the
-- other figures of a case, are stand-ins invented for the case.

§ `Cases -- the seat`

§§ `Am I eligible for Silver Support? (ss 6 and 7)`

-- On what date do I reach 65 (s 6(2)).  Arguments: year, month, day of birth (0 = not known).
-- Born 15 March 1960: the 65th anniversary is 15 March 2025.
#ASSERT `On what date do I reach 65` 1960 3 15 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2025)
-- Born on 29 February 1960: deemed to be 1 March 2025.
#ASSERT `On what date do I reach 65` 1960 2 29 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)
-- Born on 29 February 1996: 2061 is not a leap year, so 1 March 2061.
#ASSERT `On what date do I reach 65` 1996 2 29 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2061)
-- Day not known: the 1st of the month (s 6(2)(c)).
#ASSERT `On what date do I reach 65` 1960 3 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2025)
-- Month and day not known: 1 January (s 6(2)(c) and (d)).
#ASSERT `On what date do I reach 65` 1960 0 0 EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2025)
-- Not covered: the Act deems a month and a day but says nothing of a year that cannot be ascertained.
#ASSERT `On what date do I reach 65` 0 3 15 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Have I reached 65 (s 6(1)(b)).  Arguments: year, month, day of birth, date asked about.
-- The day before, the day of and the day after the 65th anniversary of 15 March 1960.
#ASSERT `Have I reached 65` 1960 3 15 (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I reached 65` 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I reached 65` 1960 3 15 (Date 16 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Born on 29 February 1960: not yet 65 on 28 February 2025, 65 on 1 March 2025.
#ASSERT `Have I reached 65` 1960 2 29 (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I reached 65` 1960 2 29 (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Year not known: not covered.
#ASSERT `Have I reached 65` 0 3 15 (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Am I an eligible individual (s 6(1)).  Arguments: citizen, year, month, day of birth, date asked about, other criteria.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible individual` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The day before the 65th birthday.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible individual` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 14 3 2025) Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a citizen.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible individual` FALSE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The prescribed criteria are not met.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible individual` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) No EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not sure whether the prescribed criteria are met: not covered.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible individual` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Year of birth not known: not covered.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible individual` TRUE 0 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) Yes EQUALS NOTHING
-- A leap-day birth, the day before and the day of the deemed anniversary.
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible individual` TRUE 1960 2 29 (Date 28 2 2025) Yes EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I an eligible individual` TRUE 1960 2 29 (Date 1 3 2025) Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE

-- Am I eligible to receive benefits (s 7(1)).  Same arguments.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive benefits` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not an eligible individual: outside the grant, which does not say such a person receives nothing.
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive benefits` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 14 3 2025) Yes EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I eligible to receive benefits` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING

-- How much am I eligible to receive (ss 7(1), (2)).  Same arguments and the amount the regulations prescribe (0 = not known); 777 is a stand-in.
#ASSERT `How much am I eligible to receive` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) Yes 777 EQUALS JUST 777
-- The amount is in regulations that are not among the sources: not known.
#ASSERT `How much am I eligible to receive` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) Yes 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How much am I eligible to receive` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 14 3 2025) Yes 777 EQUALS NOTHING

-- How and when will I be paid (s 7(1)): the Act leaves the manner to regulations, whoever asks.
#ASSERT `How and when will I be paid` TRUE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) Yes EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How and when will I be paid` FALSE 1960 3 15 (Date 15 3 2025) Yes EQUALS NOTHING

-- Does my benefit stop because of the change: the Act is silent, whatever has changed.
#ASSERT `Does my benefit stop because of the change` `I left Singapore` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my benefit stop because of the change` `I stopped being a citizen of Singapore` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my benefit stop because of the change` `My income or assets changed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does my benefit stop because of the change` `Something else changed` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `What the authorities may do with my information (ss 8 and 9)`

-- Is the authorised person barred (s 8(3)).  Arguments: what was done, I opted out, they were told, I consented.
#ASSERT `Is the authorised person barred` `accessing means information about the individual obtained under section 8(1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the authorised person barred` `using or disclosing under section 9 means information about the individual that was previously accessed` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I consented.
#ASSERT `Is the authorised person barred` `accessing means information about the individual obtained under section 8(1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- I did not opt out.
#ASSERT `Is the authorised person barred` `accessing means information about the individual obtained under section 8(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- They have not yet been told: the bar runs from notice, and the Act does not say what applies before.
#ASSERT `Is the authorised person barred` `accessing means information about the individual obtained under section 8(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Something else was done with the information: s 8(3) does not speak of it.
#ASSERT `Is the authorised person barred` `any other act` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Is the department protected from liability to me (s 8(4)(a)).  Arguments: passed on as directed, my opt-out barred it.
#ASSERT `Is the department protected from liability to me` TRUE No EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the department protected from liability to me` TRUE Yes EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the department protected from liability to me` TRUE `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the department protected from liability to me` FALSE No EQUALS NOTHING

-- Is breaching my opt-out an offence (s 8(6)).
#ASSERT `Is breaching my opt-out an offence` Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is breaching my opt-out an offence` No EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is breaching my opt-out an offence` `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Is it authorised to use or disclose my information (s 9(2)).  Arguments: obtained under s 8, I consented, to administer or enforce the Act, to administer the Scheme.
-- No purpose the section allows: not authorised.
#ASSERT `Is it authorised to use or disclose my information` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A purpose the section names: "only if" does not say it is then authorised.
#ASSERT `Is it authorised to use or disclose my information` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is it authorised to use or disclose my information` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- I consented: the subsection speaks of use "without the consent".
#ASSERT `Is it authorised to use or disclose my information` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not information obtained under section 8.
#ASSERT `Is it authorised to use or disclose my information` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Must the report about me stop (s 9(5)).  Arguments: who would give it, it is such a report, I opted out, they were told, I consented.
#ASSERT `Must the report about me stop` `the Commissioner for Silver Support` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the report about me stop` `the Board` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the report about me stop` `an administrator who is a public officer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- I consented, or did not opt out.
#ASSERT `Must the report about me stop` `the Board` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the report about me stop` `the Board` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not yet told.
#ASSERT `Must the report about me stop` `the Board` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Someone the section does not name, or a report of another kind.
#ASSERT `Must the report about me stop` `someone else` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must the report about me stop` `the Board` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Is it an offence to breach section 9 (s 9(7)).  Arguments: contravened s 9(2), 9(3), 9(5).
#ASSERT `Is it an offence to breach section 9` Yes No No EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it an offence to breach section 9` No No Yes EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it an offence to breach section 9` No No No EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is it an offence to breach section 9` `I am not sure` `I am not sure` `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `If I have been paid too much or not entitled (s 10)`

-- How much must I pay back (s 10(1)).  Arguments: paid as a cash grant, I was an eligible individual, I was eligible for that grant, the amount paid, the amount I was eligible to receive (0 = not known); the amounts are stand-ins.
-- Not an eligible individual: the whole amount paid.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` TRUE No `I am not sure` 100 0 EQUALS JUST 100
-- An eligible individual not eligible for that cash grant: the whole amount paid.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` TRUE Yes No 100 0 EQUALS JUST 100
-- Eligible for 60 and paid 100: the excess, 40.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` TRUE Yes Yes 100 60 EQUALS JUST 40
-- Paid exactly what I was eligible for: nothing is recoverable under this subsection.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` TRUE Yes Yes 100 100 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Not a cash grant: nothing is made recoverable by this subsection.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` FALSE No No 100 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Not sure whether I was eligible for that cash grant: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` TRUE Yes `I am not sure` 100 60 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Eligible, but the amount I was eligible to receive is not known: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` TRUE Yes Yes 100 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not sure whether I was an eligible individual, but not eligible for that cash grant: the whole amount paid, either way (limb (a)(i) if I was not an eligible individual, limb (a)(ii) if I was).
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` TRUE `I am not sure` No 1000 0 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Not sure about either: not covered.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` TRUE `I am not sure` `I am not sure` 1000 800 EQUALS NOTHING

-- How much must I pay back for a false statement (s 10(2)).  Arguments: false statement, false document, the amount obtained (a stand-in).
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back for a false statement` TRUE FALSE 500 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back for a false statement` FALSE TRUE 500 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back for a false statement` FALSE FALSE 500 EQUALS 0

-- Can the administrator take it out of what I am owed (s 10(3)).  Arguments: the body is an administrator, I owe an amount, where the money would come from.
#ASSERT `Can the administrator take it out of what I am owed` Yes TRUE `a cash grant or other benefit the recipient is eligible to receive under the Scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the administrator take it out of what I am owed` Yes TRUE `another sum payable to the recipient by the administrator` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Some other source: the sources are listed without "only".
#ASSERT `Can the administrator take it out of what I am owed` Yes TRUE `another source` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the administrator take it out of what I am owed` `I am not sure` TRUE `another sum payable to the recipient by the administrator` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the administrator take it out of what I am owed` Yes FALSE `another sum payable to the recipient by the administrator` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Offences, penalties and what I can be made to pay (ss 11 to 17)`

-- Have I committed the offence of a false statement (s 11(1)).  Arguments: false statement, false document, dishonestly obtained.
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of a false statement` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of a false statement` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of a false statement` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Have I committed the offence of a false statement` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Can the court order me to repay on conviction (s 12).
#ASSERT `Can the court order me to repay on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the court order me to repay on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the court order me to repay on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Is the certificate evidence of what I received or owe (s 13).  Arguments: purports to be issued by an administrator, certifies what I received, certifies what I owe.
#ASSERT `Is the certificate evidence of what I received or owe` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the certificate evidence of what I received or owe` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the certificate evidence of what I received or owe` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Can I be required to give information (s 14(1)).  Arguments: who is asking, why, what is asked, written notice, time and place reasonable, concerns the Scheme's benefits, they believe it is connected.
-- The Commissioner, reviewing the Scheme, by written notice at a reasonable time and place, about benefits.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give information` `the Commissioner` `reviewing the administration of the Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of a benefit` `to attend, answer a question or give a signed statement` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No written notice.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give information` `the Commissioner` `reviewing the administration of the Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of a benefit` `to attend, answer a question or give a signed statement` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Information within my knowledge, on a reasonable belief that it is connected.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give information` `the Commissioner` `reviewing the administration of the Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of a benefit` `to provide information within the person's knowledge` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No such belief.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give information` `the Commissioner` `reviewing the administration of the Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of a benefit` `to provide information within the person's knowledge` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An investigator, conducting an investigation, producing a document.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give information` `an investigator as requirer` `conducting an investigation under this Act` `to produce a document or record for inspection` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Commissioner for a purpose that is an investigator's, or someone else asking.
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give information` `the Commissioner` `conducting an investigation under this Act` `to produce a document or record for inspection` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I be required to give information` `someone else as requirer` `reviewing the administration of the Scheme or the disbursement or conferment of a benefit` `to provide information within the person's knowledge` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Must I tell the authorities about the change: the Act is silent, whatever has changed.
#ASSERT `Must I tell the authorities about the change` `I left Singapore` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I tell the authorities about the change` `I stopped being a citizen of Singapore` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I tell the authorities about the change` `My income or assets changed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I tell the authorities about the change` `Something else changed` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Have I committed an offence by not giving it in time (s 14(4)).  Arguments: who required it, under s 14(1)(b), I refused, days allowed, days counted, reasonable excuse.  7 days is a stand-in.
-- The day before the time runs out, and the last day allowed: in time.
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by not giving it in time` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE 7 6 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by not giving it in time` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE 7 7 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The day after: out of time.
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by not giving it in time` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE 7 8 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Refused, within the time.
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by not giving it in time` `an investigator as requirer` TRUE TRUE 7 1 FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Out of time, with a reasonable excuse.
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by not giving it in time` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE 7 8 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Have I committed an offence by obstructing (s 15).  Arguments: whom, obstructed, reasonable excuse.
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by obstructing` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by obstructing` `an investigator as requirer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by obstructing` `the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Have I committed an offence by obstructing` `someone else as requirer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- What is the heaviest sentence for the offence (ss 8(6), 9(7), 11(1), 14(4), 15).  Fields: greatest fine in dollars, greatest imprisonment in months.
#ASSERT `What is the heaviest sentence for the offence` `the offence in section 8(6)` EQUALS Penalty OF 5000, 12
#ASSERT `What is the heaviest sentence for the offence` `the offence in section 9(7)` EQUALS Penalty OF 5000, 12
#ASSERT `What is the heaviest sentence for the offence` `the offence in section 11(1)` EQUALS Penalty OF 5000, 12
#ASSERT `What is the heaviest sentence for the offence` `the offence in section 14(4)` EQUALS Penalty OF 10000, 6
#ASSERT `What is the heaviest sentence for the offence` `the offence in section 15` EQUALS Penalty OF 20000, 12

-- Am I guilty of the body corporate's offence (s 16(1)).  Arguments: kind of body, offence proved, my position, consent or connivance, neglect.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the body corporate's offence` `an ordinary body corporate` TRUE `a director` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the body corporate's offence` `a limited liability partnership as defined in section 2(1) of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` TRUE `a manager` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the body corporate's offence` `an ordinary body corporate` FALSE `a director` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the body corporate's offence` `an ordinary body corporate` TRUE `no such position` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Am I treated as a director (s 16(2)).
#ASSERT `Am I treated as a director` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I treated as a director` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Am I guilty of the partnership's offence (s 16(3)).  Arguments: kind of body, offence proved, I am a partner, I purported to act as a partner, consent, neglect.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the partnership's offence` `a partnership` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the partnership's offence` `a partnership` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the partnership's offence` `a partnership` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Am I guilty of the association's offence (s 16(4)).  Arguments: kind of body, offence proved, my position, governing body member, consent, neglect.
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the association's offence` `an unincorporated association other than a partnership` TRUE `the president` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the association's offence` `an unincorporated association other than a partnership` TRUE `no such position in the association` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I guilty of the association's offence` `an unincorporated association other than a partnership` TRUE `no such position in the association` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- What is the most I can be asked to pay to settle (s 17(1)).  Arguments: the offence, the offence is prescribed as compoundable.
-- Every offence of the Act has a maximum fine of $5,000 or more, one half of which is above $1,000, so the lower is $1,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be asked to pay to settle` `the offence in section 8(6)` Yes EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be asked to pay to settle` `the offence in section 11(1)` Yes EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be asked to pay to settle` `the offence in section 15` Yes EQUALS JUST 1000
-- Not prescribed as compoundable, or not known: not covered (the regulations are outside the sources).
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be asked to pay to settle` `the offence in section 11(1)` No EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be asked to pay to settle` `the offence in section 11(1)` `I am not sure` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Are further proceedings barred once I have paid (s 17(2)).
#ASSERT `Are further proceedings barred once I have paid` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are further proceedings barred once I have paid` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Can I hold an official personally liable? (s 19)`

-- Is the official protected from personal liability (s 19).  Arguments: who, good faith, reasonable care, in executing the Act.
#ASSERT `Is the official protected from personal liability` `the Commissioner for Silver Support` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the official protected from personal liability` `an administrator who is a public officer` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the official protected from personal liability` `a member, officer or employee of an administrator that is a public authority other than the Board` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not in good faith, or without reasonable care: outside the protection.
#ASSERT `Is the official protected from personal liability` `an investigator` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the official protected from personal liability` `an investigator` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Board itself is not an individual the section lists; nor is someone it does not name.
#ASSERT `Is the official protected from personal liability` `the Board` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is the official protected from personal liability` `someone else` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Does section 19 leave the liability in place (s 19(4)).
#ASSERT `Does section 19 leave the liability in place` `liability under section 20 of the Financial Procedure Act 1966` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 19 leave the liability in place` `liability under section 8(6)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 19 leave the liability in place` `liability under section 9(7)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 19 leave the liability in place` `any other liability` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `What the regulations may cover (s 20)`

-- Can regulations deal with the matter (s 20(2)): when payment is made or stops (terms and conditions) and a review of an assessment.
#ASSERT `Can regulations deal with the matter` `the terms and conditions for each benefit under the Scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can regulations deal with the matter` `the review by the Commissioner of any assessment, and the time within which the application for the review must be made` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can regulations deal with the matter` `the benefits under the Scheme, including different amounts of benefits for different classes of eligible individuals` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A matter that s 20(2) does not list: s 20(1) may or may not cover it.
#ASSERT `Can regulations deal with the matter` `another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
